{"title":"Topicwise Test-1 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 ME Strength of Materials-1","fileName":"051_Topicwise Test-1 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 ME Strength of Materials-1.html","branch":"MECHANICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Mechanical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>An elastomeric bearing pad consisting of two steel plates bounded to a chlorophene elastomer, is subjected to a shear force V during a static loading test as shown in figure. The pad has dimensions <em>a</em> = <em>b</em> = 200 mm, and the elastomer has thickness <em>t</em> = 40 mm. When the force F equals 20 kN, the top plate is found to have displaced laterally 10.00 mm with respect to the bottom<br />\nplate. The shear modulus of elasticity G of the chlorophene is ______ MPa.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/2db2ac540ef79651dbb04f830cadb64f2dbded74.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>2 (2 - 2)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c27d3123980df3f8fb369bf106e11de07cd11d3d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two solid cylindrical rods <em>AB</em> and <em>BC</em> are welded together at <em>B</em> and loaded as shown in figure.<br />\nIf the average normal stress must not exceed 200 MPa in either rod, the allowable values of the<br />\ndiameter <em>d</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>d</em><sub>2</sub> are</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/9db7ea016dfb2847fcd86f4a9732b3625854060d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>d</em><sub>1</sub> = 45.2 mm, <em>d</em><sub>2</sub> = 20.1 mm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <em>d</em><sub>1</sub> = 22.6 mm, <em>d</em><sub>2</sub> = 40.2 mm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <em>d</em><sub>1</sub> = 20.1 mm, <em>d</em><sub>2</sub> = 45.2 mm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <em>d</em><sub>1</sub> = 17.8 mm, <em>d</em><sub>2</sub> = 30.9 mm</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ffc369761bb7ce45152b3956acc344a4b34848a5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A steel bar 0.5 m long and cross-section of 10 mm × 50 mm is compressed under an axial load of 100 kN applied in the direction of its length. If net strain in one direction is prevented by applying a suitable compressive load, then the absolute change in length will be _____ mm.<br />\n[Take <em>E</em> = 210 GPa and μ = 0.3] (Correct upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.43","high":"0.43"},"solution":"<p>0.43 (0.40 - 0.45)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a1d75ef293b9bc20194154ed5c588024eb5dd7b2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8b0c3e611393ae84bab15134d189ec055da9ac87.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two solid members are joined together using a 60° scarf weld <em>AB</em> as shown in figure. The average normal and average shear stress resisted in the plane of the weld are</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a827ed6a84218c812795c4cc180fa0f845ace249.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/afa236f58a003825dcebf96eb351290c5bc4805e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/2d9669c9d64fff59b02a0661ea01525fe966dbdc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8d37bbb4bb2c5c4f2c188bef13b5d5a39c991f51.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img sr